---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Notice from '../components/Notice.astro';
import { LINKS, SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Mission, openness and governance of Open Workplace Commons.">
  <PageHeader title="About Open Workplace Commons" lede={SITE.tagline} />

  <div class="container section">
    <h2>Mission</h2>
    <p>
      Many organizations build the same workplace training independently. OWC is a
      community-maintained, freely reusable foundation for workplace education: curricula,
      competencies, lessons, practice questions with answers, and non-binding evaluation guidance.
      We want it to be a lasting public resource and not a proprietary learning platform.
    </p>

    <h2>Openness</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>One source of truth.</strong> Content lives in the public
        <a href={LINKS.curricula}>curricula repository</a>. This portal presents it and does not own
        it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Tool-neutral.</strong> Content is plain Markdown and YAML so any LMS, authoring tool
        or site can use it. Nothing requires this portal or any OWC-affiliated product.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Traceable.</strong> References, authorship, reviewer scope and revision history are
        kept with the content.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Governance</h2>
    <p>
      Governance is still being defined. The draft design describes editorial maintainers,
      subject-matter reviewers, curriculum reviewers and release maintainers, with independent
      review for substantive changes. Reviewer thresholds, escalation, and the final content and
      software licenses are open decisions. See the
      <a href={`${LINKS.curricula}/blob/main/docs/08-roadmap-and-decisions.md`}>open questions</a>.
    </p>

    <Notice title="What OWC does not do">
      <p>
        OWC does not run certification exams, keep secret official exam banks, issue credentials,
        accredit providers or record learner results. Adopting organizations choose how to deliver
        and evaluate training and may issue their own completion records. OWC does not guarantee
        that generic content meets any employer's regulatory or compliance requirements.
      </p>
    </Notice>

    <h2>Interoperability</h2>
    <p>
      Formats such as SCORM, QTI, CASE and LTI are interoperability <em>targets</em> in the draft
      specification. None is supported or claimed to conform yet.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
